{"name":"Blonde Wood","hex":"#ab7741","fetched":"2026-10-11","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"blonde","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of blond (“person with fair hair”).","Alternative form of blond (“color”)"]},{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Alternative form of blond.","Stupid, ignorant, naive."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/blonde"},{"term":"wood","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["The substance making up the central part of the trunk and branches of a tree. Used as a material for construction, to manufacture various items, etc. or as fuel.","The wood from a particular species of tree."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To cover or plant with trees.","To hide behind trees."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/wood"}],"entries":[{"title":"Blond","blocks":[{"text":"Blond or blonde, also referred to as fair hair, is a human hair color characterized by low levels of eumelanin, the dark pigment. The resultant visible hue depends on various factors, but always has some yellowish color. The color can be from the very pale blond to reddish \"strawberry\" blond or golden-brownish (\"sandy\") blond colors. Occasionally, the state of being blond, and specifically the occurrence of blond traits in a predominantly dark or colored population are referred to as blondism."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg/330px-Lars-Unnerstall2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blond"},{"title":"Wood","blocks":[{"text":"Wood is a structural tissue/material found as xylem in the stems and roots of trees and other woody plants. Being a natural material, it is characterized as an organic material – a natural composite of cellulosic fibers that are strong in tension and embedded in a matrix of lignin and hemicelluloses that resists compression."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/16_wood_samples.jpg/330px-16_wood_samples.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wood"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/500px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/1280px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/ea/Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg/500px-Anonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_%28detail%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Detail of a portrait of Sigismund Casimir Vasa (c. 1644), with characteristic blond hair which darkened with time as confirmed by his later effigies","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AAnonymous_Ferdinand_of_Austria_in_Hungarian_costume_(detail).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Klara_Gadd.jpg/500px-Klara_Gadd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Klara_Gadd.jpg/1280px-Klara_Gadd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/8f/Klara_Gadd.jpg/500px-Klara_Gadd.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Actress Klara Gadd has strawberry blonde hair","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AKlara_Gadd.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/b